1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,130
You did not wake up into silence.

2
00:00:02,130 --> 00:00:08,200
You woke up in the middle of a conversation that had already started without you, and you were already losing it.

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:11,100
It says you should have handled yesterday better.

4
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:14,920
It says you are behind before you have even begun.

5
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:19,050
It says the thing you have been asking God for is still not here.

6
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:22,910
The trouble this morning is not that your mind is loud.

7
00:00:22,910 --> 00:00:25,950
The trouble is which voice gets to speak first.

8
00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:30,090
And one voice has been speaking since long before you opened your eyes.

9
00:00:30,090 --> 00:00:34,730
So wherever you are right now, close your eyes if you can.

10
00:00:34,730 --> 00:00:39,500
Take one slow breath, and let your shoulders come down.

11
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,010
Do not try to quiet everything.

12
00:00:42,010 --> 00:00:44,580
Just invite God into this moment.

13
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:47,710
Listen to how David prayed on a morning like this.

14
00:00:47,710 --> 00:00:58,340
In Psalm one hundred forty-three, verse eight, he said, "Let the morning bring me word of your unfailing love, for I have put my trust in you.

15
00:00:58,340 --> 00:01:08,180
Show me the way I should go, for to you I entrust my life." He wrote that while he was being hunted, with no idea which way to go.

16
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:10,900
This is not a video you watch.

17
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:13,080
It is a morning you keep.

18
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:20,020
If you want to begin every morning this way, with his voice first, subscribe and pray with us tomorrow.

19
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:29,920
So before we ask God for anything, let us set down the loudest voice, let his love speak first, and ask him to show us the way through today.

20
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:34,670
I have not stepped into this day yet, and I am already tired of it.

21
00:01:34,670 --> 00:01:47,030
Somewhere between opening my eyes and sitting up, I ran the whole day in my head, every task, every conversation, every hour I do not think I have enough strength for.

22
00:01:47,030 --> 00:01:49,650
I carried a day I have not lived yet.

23
00:01:49,650 --> 00:01:51,830
Take it off my shoulders.

24
00:01:51,830 --> 00:01:55,870
Your word tells me something different about this morning.

25
00:01:55,870 --> 00:02:08,470
In Lamentations chapter three, verses twenty-two and twenty-three, it says, "Because of the Lord's great love we are not consumed, for his compassions never fail.

26
00:02:08,470 --> 00:02:13,140
They are new every morning; great is your faithfulness."

27
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:15,150
New every morning.

28
00:02:15,150 --> 00:02:17,240
Not renewed for the strong.

29
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:20,500
Not reserved for the ones who prayed better yesterday.

30
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:23,600
This mercy has never been used before.

31
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:25,350
No one has spent it.

32
00:02:25,350 --> 00:02:28,200
It has been waiting here since before I woke.

33
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:35,780
So I want to stop treating today as a weight I have to survive, and start seeing it as a place you are already standing in.

34
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:39,180
You are not waiting at the end of this day to see how I did.

35
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:41,070
You are here at the beginning.

36
00:02:41,070 --> 00:02:45,600
And if your mercy is new this morning, then there is something new to hear this morning.

37
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:49,450
Mercy that new has to be spoken before I can hear it.

38
00:02:49,450 --> 00:02:53,450
Let the morning bring me word of your unfailing love.

39
00:02:53,450 --> 00:02:56,530
Teach me why David asked for that first.

40
00:02:56,530 --> 00:02:58,670
He was hiding when he prayed it.

41
00:02:58,670 --> 00:03:04,410
He needed rescue, food, a way out, and he asked for love before any of it.

42
00:03:04,410 --> 00:03:06,400
Why love first?

43
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:12,870
Because rescue tells him what you will do, and love tells him who he belongs to.

44
00:03:12,870 --> 00:03:17,140
Someone can be rescued and still not know they are wanted.

45
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:22,430
So he asked for the harder thing, the thing that changes how he hears everything else that day.

46
00:03:22,430 --> 00:03:25,680
Then he said, show me the way I should go.

47
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:27,710
Not the way I want to go.

48
00:03:27,710 --> 00:03:30,350
Not the way that will hurt the least.

49
00:03:30,350 --> 00:03:34,570
There is a difference, and I usually pretend there is not.

50
00:03:34,570 --> 00:03:38,560
The way I want is the one I have already chosen before I prayed.

51
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:45,940
The way I should go is the one I have to be shown, which means I have to be willing to be told something I did not plan for.

52
00:03:45,940 --> 00:03:50,700
And then the last line, for to you I entrust my life.

53
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:55,690
What does it mean to hand you my life when I still cannot see how any of it turns out?

54
00:03:55,690 --> 00:04:07,000
David wrote in Psalm chapter five, verse three, "In the morning, Lord, you hear my voice; in the morning I lay my requests before you and wait expectantly."

55
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,420
He lays it down, and then he waits.

56
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:13,220
The trust is not in the answer arriving.

57
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:15,740
The trust is in who is holding it.

58
00:04:15,740 --> 00:04:18,100
But you were speaking before I asked.

59
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:21,220
You spoke all night while I slept.

60
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:24,340
Thank you for the hours I have no memory of.

61
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:27,310
Last night I let go of everything.

62
00:04:27,310 --> 00:04:29,220
I stopped deciding.

63
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:31,380
I stopped watching the door.

64
00:04:31,380 --> 00:04:40,020
For six or seven hours I was as helpless as I have ever been, and I was not afraid, because I was not awake to be afraid.

65
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:43,940
You kept my breathing going in a room where nobody was in charge.

66
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:46,750
You counted the beats I never counted.

67
00:04:46,750 --> 00:04:52,750
There were hours last night when I was completely unable to protect myself, and nothing came for me.

68
00:04:52,750 --> 00:04:55,160
I do not know what did not happen.

69
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:57,380
I only know I woke up.

70
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:59,100
That was not luck.

71
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:02,780
That was you, working in a room I was not conscious in.

72
00:05:02,780 --> 00:05:05,490
And you did not do it because I asked.

73
00:05:05,490 --> 00:05:08,110
I did not pray my way through the night.

74
00:05:08,110 --> 00:05:10,800
I was not thanking you at two in the morning.

75
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:16,900
I was not aware of you at all, and you did not step back when my attention went out.

76
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:19,270
This is what I keep learning about you.

77
00:05:19,270 --> 00:05:22,800
Your faithfulness is not a response to my attention.

78
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:26,900
It does not rise when I notice it and fall when I forget.

79
00:05:26,900 --> 00:05:35,730
Your compassions never fail, and they never failed last night, in the dark, with no one thanking you and no one watching.

80
00:05:35,730 --> 00:05:38,850
You were good in a room with no audience.

81
00:05:38,850 --> 00:05:42,550
So you were already speaking before I said a word this morning.

82
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:45,080
That is what I am starting to understand.

83
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:51,050
You did not wait for me to become the kind of person who deserved to be kept, and then keep me.

84
00:05:51,050 --> 00:05:58,950
You did not wait until I had prayed enough, or fixed the thing I keep not fixing, or become gentler with the people I live with.

85
00:05:58,950 --> 00:06:00,650
You went first.

86
00:06:00,650 --> 00:06:02,870
You always go first.

87
00:06:02,870 --> 00:06:09,000
Before I had one clear thought this morning, your kindness had already been at work for hours.

88
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:13,650
I did not earn a single one of those hours, and you gave me all of them.

89
00:06:13,650 --> 00:06:19,890
And now, before I ask you for anything, I want to say something that has nothing to do with what I need.

90
00:06:19,890 --> 00:06:21,820
You are good, Father.

91
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:23,360
Not useful to me.

92
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:24,720
Good.

93
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:28,550
You are steady in a way that nothing in my life is steady.

94
00:06:28,550 --> 00:06:31,680
You do not have moods I have to manage.

95
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:39,810
You are the same this morning as you were the morning I was full of faith, and the same as the morning I could not feel anything at all.

96
00:06:39,810 --> 00:06:43,470
I would rather have you than the things I want from you.

97
00:06:43,470 --> 00:06:49,680
If everything I am about to pray for was answered and you were not here, it would not be enough.

98
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:54,740
And if you have been speaking all along, then I do not need to speak louder.

99
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:57,970
I need to put down what is already talking.

100
00:06:57,970 --> 00:07:02,900
There are things from yesterday I do not want to carry into today.

101
00:07:02,900 --> 00:07:06,330
I said something to someone who did not deserve it.

102
00:07:06,330 --> 00:07:11,530
I heard it come out of my mouth and I watched them get smaller, and I did not stop.

103
00:07:11,530 --> 00:07:19,230
I was short with the person who is easiest to be short with, the one who is always there, the one who will not leave over it.

104
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:22,810
I knew what I should have done and I did not do it.

105
00:07:22,810 --> 00:07:24,910
Not because I forgot.

106
00:07:24,910 --> 00:07:29,580
I decided not to, and then I told myself I was tired.

107
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:31,770
I am not going to soften that.

108
00:07:31,770 --> 00:07:35,240
I am not going to explain it into something smaller.

109
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:40,080
It was wrong, and I am the one who did it, and I am asking you to forgive me.

110
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:41,880
Not to overlook it.

111
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:43,340
To forgive it.

112
00:07:43,340 --> 00:07:46,900
And now I have to do the part I always skip.

113
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:54,050
I usually confess and keep walking, because staying still long enough to be forgiven feels like too much to accept.

114
00:07:54,050 --> 00:07:56,360
So I am staying here for a moment.

115
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:57,930
You forgive me.

116
00:07:57,930 --> 00:08:00,430
Not because today will be better.

117
00:08:00,430 --> 00:08:02,650
Not because I promised anything.

118
00:08:02,650 --> 00:08:04,640
Because of who you are.

119
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:09,026
You are not a God who forgives me and then reminds me of it later.

120
00:08:09,026 --> 00:08:10,696
I receive it.

121
00:08:10,696 --> 00:08:14,976
I am not going to argue with you about whether I am allowed to have it.

122
00:08:14,976 --> 00:08:19,616
You have already answered that, and yesterday is not the judge of this morning.

123
00:08:19,616 --> 00:08:25,056
So I am putting yesterday down, right here, before anything else gets said.

124
00:08:25,056 --> 00:08:28,596
The shame that woke up with me, I am handing to you.

125
00:08:28,596 --> 00:08:33,046
The sentence I keep reading over myself, I am handing to you.

126
00:08:33,046 --> 00:08:40,566
The version of me that showed up yesterday, the one I do not like, the one I would take back if I could, I am giving all of

127
00:08:40,566 --> 00:08:43,516
that to you instead of hiding it.

128
00:08:43,516 --> 00:08:51,246
That message from last night is still sitting there unanswered, and it is unanswered because I do not know what kind of person I am when I answer it.

129
00:08:51,246 --> 00:08:54,826
I am not going to spend today defending yesterday.

130
00:08:54,826 --> 00:08:56,376
It happened.

131
00:08:56,376 --> 00:08:58,156
You have dealt with it.

132
00:08:58,156 --> 00:09:00,956
It does not get to speak first anymore.

133
00:09:00,956 --> 00:09:09,616
So the loudest voice is on the floor now, and where it was, there is quiet, and quiet needs something said into it.

134
00:09:09,616 --> 00:09:14,256
So say it to me now, before this day says anything else.

135
00:09:14,256 --> 00:09:19,406
Your unfailing love, out loud, over me, this morning.

136
00:09:19,406 --> 00:09:23,556
Because it will not be the first thing I hear if you do not speak it.

137
00:09:23,556 --> 00:09:27,126
The first thing I heard today was a number.

138
00:09:27,126 --> 00:09:28,766
How much is left.

139
00:09:28,766 --> 00:09:30,826
How far behind I am.

140
00:09:30,826 --> 00:09:34,066
How much of yesterday's list moved into today's list.

141
00:09:34,066 --> 00:09:36,166
That is how I measure myself.

142
00:09:36,166 --> 00:09:38,776
Finished, or not finished.

143
00:09:38,776 --> 00:09:44,666
And this morning the list is longer than it was yesterday, so the voice has already decided what I am worth.

144
00:09:44,666 --> 00:09:50,446
It has already told me I am falling behind, and it said it before my feet were on the floor.

145
00:09:50,446 --> 00:09:52,556
But your love is unfailing.

146
00:09:52,556 --> 00:09:55,286
I want to sit inside that word for a second.

147
00:09:55,286 --> 00:09:59,216
Unfailing does not mean strong.

148
00:09:59,216 --> 00:10:01,516
It means it does not react.

149
00:10:01,516 --> 00:10:06,016
It does not go up when I have a productive day and down when I waste one.

150
00:10:06,016 --> 00:10:10,066
It did not change last night while I was doing nothing at all.

151
00:10:10,066 --> 00:10:13,326
You are not comparing me to who I was yesterday.

152
00:10:13,326 --> 00:10:15,556
You are not adding up the week.

153
00:10:15,556 --> 00:10:18,426
So speak to me before anyone else does.

154
00:10:18,426 --> 00:10:29,256
Before the first message, before the first request, before I have accomplished one thing that would make me feel like I am allowed to be here, tell me I am yours.

155
00:10:29,256 --> 00:10:35,566
Say it in the car on the way in, when the day has not started well and there is still an hour of driving left.

156
00:10:35,566 --> 00:10:40,656
Say it when I open the laptop and the first thing on the screen is something I am behind on.

157
00:10:40,656 --> 00:10:45,806
Say it when I see that message I still have not answered and my stomach drops.

158
00:10:45,806 --> 00:10:51,876
And when I look in the mirror and the first sentence in my head is not a kind one, say it again then.

159
00:10:51,876 --> 00:10:55,316
I am not asking you to make me feel good about myself.

160
00:10:55,316 --> 00:10:58,266
I am asking you to change what I am measuring.

161
00:10:58,266 --> 00:11:05,806
Because if I walk out of this room measuring what I got done, this day already has a verdict on it and I have not lived it yet.

162
00:11:05,806 --> 00:11:14,236
But if I walk out measuring how loved I am, then nothing I get done today can raise it and nothing I fail at today can lower it.

163
00:11:14,236 --> 00:11:16,686
That is a different kind of morning.

164
00:11:16,686 --> 00:11:19,776
That is a different kind of person walking into it.

165
00:11:19,776 --> 00:11:25,906
And someone who knows they are loved can finally ask a question they have been avoiding.

166
00:11:25,906 --> 00:11:31,896
Because now, if you answer, I know it will not come back as a scolding.

167
00:11:31,896 --> 00:11:34,566
So I can ask you which way to go.

168
00:11:34,566 --> 00:11:37,906
I do not know what I am doing today.

169
00:11:37,906 --> 00:11:40,386
Not in the dramatic way.

170
00:11:40,386 --> 00:11:48,446
In the ordinary way, where I have to pick, and both options look reasonable, and I have been going back and forth for three days.

171
00:11:48,446 --> 00:11:51,316
There is a decision I have to answer today.

172
00:11:51,316 --> 00:11:52,926
Not tomorrow.

173
00:11:52,926 --> 00:11:54,286
Today.

174
00:11:54,286 --> 00:11:59,666
And I cannot tell which one is wisdom and which one is just the one I am more afraid of.

175
00:11:59,666 --> 00:12:10,946
Your word says, in Proverbs chapter three, verses five and six, "Trust in the Lord with all your heart and lean not on your own understanding;

176
00:12:10,946 --> 00:12:15,886
in all your ways submit to him, and he will make your paths straight."

177
00:12:15,886 --> 00:12:18,926
I notice what that verse does not say.

178
00:12:18,926 --> 00:12:21,716
It does not say the road gets easy.

179
00:12:21,716 --> 00:12:25,326
It does not say the hard thing is removed from the road.

180
00:12:25,326 --> 00:12:26,916
It says straight.

181
00:12:26,916 --> 00:12:28,186
Clear.

182
00:12:28,186 --> 00:12:30,766
A direction I can actually walk.

183
00:12:30,766 --> 00:12:34,616
And the part that is mine is the part I keep skipping.

184
00:12:34,616 --> 00:12:37,366
It is the not leaning on my own understanding.

185
00:12:37,366 --> 00:12:43,666
Because my understanding is what I have been leaning on all week, and it is why I am still standing here with nothing decided.

186
00:12:43,666 --> 00:12:46,256
So show me the way I should go, Lord.

187
00:12:46,256 --> 00:12:49,146
Not confirm the way I already picked.

188
00:12:49,146 --> 00:12:55,036
Show me before I decide, not after, when I am only asking you to sign something.

189
00:12:55,036 --> 00:13:00,696
There is a conversation I have been avoiding for days, and today it finds me.

190
00:13:00,696 --> 00:13:02,656
Tell me what to say in it.

191
00:13:02,656 --> 00:13:05,316
Tell me the first sentence.

192
00:13:05,316 --> 00:13:07,416
Tell me when to stop talking.

193
00:13:07,416 --> 00:13:12,036
Tell me whether the thing I want to say is honest or just something I want to win.

194
00:13:12,036 --> 00:13:17,426
And there is a person I will be near today, and I get tense before I even see them.

195
00:13:17,426 --> 00:13:20,756
I do not need you to change them by lunchtime.

196
00:13:20,756 --> 00:13:25,636
Show me where to give way and where to stand still, because I get those two backwards.

197
00:13:25,636 --> 00:13:28,616
I am not asking for the whole road.

198
00:13:28,616 --> 00:13:34,306
I have asked for the whole road before, and I think I was really asking for a guarantee.

199
00:13:34,306 --> 00:13:36,596
I am asking for the next step.

200
00:13:36,596 --> 00:13:40,856
One step, at the hour I actually need it, is enough.

201
00:13:40,856 --> 00:13:44,026
And if I am wrong today, correct me early.

202
00:13:44,026 --> 00:13:48,836
I would rather be corrected at nine in the morning than defended all day.

203
00:13:48,836 --> 00:13:54,416
Because I would rather move slowly with you than quickly by myself.

204
00:13:54,416 --> 00:13:58,416
So let me be honest about the part of my life you have not answered.

205
00:13:58,416 --> 00:14:04,686
There are rooms in my life where nothing has changed in months, and I have to say that out loud too.

206
00:14:04,686 --> 00:14:07,876
This is the same prayer I prayed yesterday.

207
00:14:07,876 --> 00:14:09,986
And the morning before that.

208
00:14:09,986 --> 00:14:16,456
And a hundred mornings I cannot count, in the same words, about the same thing, and nothing has moved.

209
00:14:16,456 --> 00:14:20,966
I know what I am about to say before I say it, and so do you.

210
00:14:20,966 --> 00:14:23,206
That is the part nobody talks about.

211
00:14:23,206 --> 00:14:26,046
It is not the waiting that wears me down.

212
00:14:26,046 --> 00:14:31,416
It is having to ask again, out loud, after asking so many times already.

213
00:14:31,416 --> 00:14:39,646
There is a kind of tiredness that comes from hope, and it is heavier than the tiredness that comes from work.

214
00:14:39,646 --> 00:14:45,056
David wrote that he lays his requests before you in the morning and waits expectantly.

215
00:14:45,056 --> 00:14:46,636
He said wait.

216
00:14:46,636 --> 00:14:49,306
He did not say receive today.

217
00:14:49,306 --> 00:14:54,576
And he still called the waiting expectant, which means he was not waiting for you to become good.

218
00:14:54,576 --> 00:14:56,536
He already knew you were.

219
00:14:56,536 --> 00:14:58,746
So here it is again, Father.

220
00:14:58,746 --> 00:15:03,546
The thing I have carried into this room every morning for longer than I want to admit.

221
00:15:03,546 --> 00:15:06,766
I am not going to demand that today is the day.

222
00:15:06,766 --> 00:15:12,876
I have tried praying like that, and when the evening came and nothing had changed, it cost me something.

223
00:15:12,876 --> 00:15:15,186
So I am asking for something else.

224
00:15:15,186 --> 00:15:18,406
Give me the strength to trust you for one day.

225
00:15:18,406 --> 00:15:19,806
Today.

226
00:15:19,806 --> 00:15:24,476
Not for the whole stretch ahead, just the hours in front of me.

227
00:15:24,476 --> 00:15:26,956
Keep the waiting from hardening me.

228
00:15:26,956 --> 00:15:31,066
That is what I am most afraid of, more than the answer never coming.

229
00:15:31,066 --> 00:15:36,806
I am afraid of becoming someone who still says the words and no longer believes them.

230
00:15:36,806 --> 00:15:38,986
Someone careful with you.

231
00:15:38,986 --> 00:15:43,816
Someone who stops asking, just to avoid being disappointed again.

232
00:15:43,816 --> 00:15:46,896
Do not let me protect myself from you like that.

233
00:15:46,896 --> 00:15:51,976
And when I cannot see anything happening, help me trust that you are not idle.

234
00:15:51,976 --> 00:15:55,906
I do not say that as a guarantee about my situation.

235
00:15:55,906 --> 00:16:01,486
I say it because of who you have been in every dark room I have ever been in.

236
00:16:01,486 --> 00:16:04,696
For the one waiting on a result that has not come.

237
00:16:04,696 --> 00:16:07,556
For the one waiting for a family to speak again.

238
00:16:07,556 --> 00:16:12,362
For the one waiting on a change in someone they love, who has not changed.

239
00:16:12,362 --> 00:16:16,532
I am one of them, and I entrust my life to you anyway.

240
00:16:16,532 --> 00:16:18,772
Not because I understand it.

241
00:16:18,772 --> 00:16:21,562
Because you are the one holding it.

242
00:16:21,562 --> 00:16:26,692
And if I am honest, what I want most this morning is not the answer.

243
00:16:26,692 --> 00:16:29,022
It is to stop waiting alone.

244
00:16:29,022 --> 00:16:31,262
You are already in the waiting with me.

245
00:16:31,262 --> 00:16:35,792
And I am not the only one who woke up inside that conversation this morning.

246
00:16:35,792 --> 00:16:39,322
Father, this next part is not about me.

247
00:16:39,322 --> 00:16:45,702
If you are still praying with me, stay for this one, because someone needs it more than I do.

248
00:16:45,702 --> 00:16:51,972
Somewhere right now, other people are lying in the dark with the same weight, and I am bringing them with me.

249
00:16:51,972 --> 00:16:55,432
Pray with me for the ones who woke up already spent.

250
00:16:55,432 --> 00:17:01,212
The one who works two jobs and slept five hours and has to be pleasant to strangers in an hour.

251
00:17:01,212 --> 00:17:08,782
The mother who has not had a morning to herself in years, whose first thought was not about her own life but about who needs feeding.

252
00:17:08,782 --> 00:17:16,722
The one caring for a parent who is disappearing slowly, who cannot remember the last time anyone asked how they are doing.

253
00:17:16,722 --> 00:17:19,712
They do not need a longer list of things to do for you.

254
00:17:19,712 --> 00:17:25,672
Let the morning bring them word of your unfailing love before it brings them another demand.

255
00:17:25,672 --> 00:17:29,572
Let something in them soften before the day starts pulling.

256
00:17:29,572 --> 00:17:34,422
And pray with me for the ones whose first voice this morning was an accusation.

257
00:17:34,422 --> 00:17:40,962
The one who has done something they have told nobody, who wakes up to it before they wake up to anything else.

258
00:17:40,962 --> 00:17:48,382
The one who thinks she used up her welcome with you a long time ago, and now prays like a stranger asking for directions.

259
00:17:48,382 --> 00:17:53,912
The one who cannot say the word forgiven about themselves, only about other people.

260
00:17:53,912 --> 00:17:56,762
Tell them what you told me before I earned anything.

261
00:17:56,762 --> 00:18:01,202
Say it slowly, because shame does not hear well.

262
00:18:01,202 --> 00:18:05,352
Let them find out this morning that you were never the voice accusing them.

263
00:18:05,352 --> 00:18:09,252
And pray with me for the ones who have been asking a long time.

264
00:18:09,252 --> 00:18:11,572
Years, some of them.

265
00:18:11,572 --> 00:18:17,122
The same words at the same table, and the situation has not moved an inch.

266
00:18:17,122 --> 00:18:22,312
The ones who are starting to wonder whether they were ever heard, and who feel guilty for wondering.

267
00:18:22,312 --> 00:18:24,612
Do not let their hope wear out.

268
00:18:24,612 --> 00:18:27,502
Hold the ones who are close to putting it down.

269
00:18:27,502 --> 00:18:31,792
Show them the way to go today, even if you are not showing them the ending yet.

270
00:18:31,792 --> 00:18:34,902
Give them one step and enough love to take it.

271
00:18:34,902 --> 00:18:38,392
And meet them in the waiting the way you have met me in mine.

272
00:18:38,392 --> 00:18:43,082
And there is someone listening right now who has not said a single word with us.

273
00:18:43,082 --> 00:18:45,032
Not out of stubbornness.

274
00:18:45,032 --> 00:18:47,112
There is nothing left to say.

275
00:18:47,112 --> 00:18:54,092
You opened this because you could not pray, and you needed a voice in the room that was not the one in your head.

276
00:18:54,092 --> 00:18:56,822
You have been sitting there while we prayed.

277
00:18:56,822 --> 00:18:58,742
So let me pray for you.

278
00:18:58,742 --> 00:19:01,412
Father, this one cannot speak this morning.

279
00:19:01,412 --> 00:19:07,002
Hear the silence as a prayer, because you know what is underneath it better than words would say it.

280
00:19:07,002 --> 00:19:10,442
Come and sit with the one who has run out of language.

281
00:19:10,442 --> 00:19:13,362
Speak first, since they cannot.

282
00:19:13,362 --> 00:19:19,482
Let your love be the first thing they hear today, before they can manage a single sentence back to you.

283
00:19:19,482 --> 00:19:23,702
You have never needed a well-said prayer to move toward someone.

284
00:19:23,702 --> 00:19:27,722
And what I am asking for them, I have to choose for myself.

285
00:19:27,722 --> 00:19:30,352
I choose to believe you this morning.

286
00:19:30,352 --> 00:19:32,952
Not because anything has been settled.

287
00:19:32,952 --> 00:19:34,982
Nothing has been settled.

288
00:19:34,982 --> 00:19:43,232
The decision is still there, the message is still unanswered, and the thing I have waited years for is still not here.

289
00:19:43,232 --> 00:19:47,042
I choose you anyway, and here is what I am choosing.

290
00:19:47,042 --> 00:19:51,982
If you can, say these with me, out loud, even quietly.

291
00:19:51,982 --> 00:19:59,692
I trust that I am loved before I accomplish anything today, and that nothing I do between now and tonight will move that.

292
00:19:59,692 --> 00:20:05,302
I trust that you will show me the way I should go when I stop leaning on my own understanding,

293
00:20:05,302 --> 00:20:09,042
even if you show me one step at a time and no further.

294
00:20:09,042 --> 00:20:11,532
I trust you where you have not answered me.

295
00:20:11,532 --> 00:20:13,490
That is the hard one.

296
00:20:13,490 --> 00:20:19,650
Your silence there is not neglect, and you have not gone quiet because you stopped caring.

297
00:20:19,650 --> 00:20:23,450
Let the morning bring me word of your unfailing love.

298
00:20:23,450 --> 00:20:24,960
It has.

299
00:20:24,960 --> 00:20:27,120
Show me the way I should go.

300
00:20:27,120 --> 00:20:28,880
You will.

301
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:31,320
To you I entrust my life.

302
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:32,730
I do.

303
00:20:32,730 --> 00:20:38,060
And believing you is not the whole of it, so I am going to do something about it today.

304
00:20:38,060 --> 00:20:40,150
I am going to answer that message.

305
00:20:40,150 --> 00:20:42,600
Today, not tomorrow.

306
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:46,280
Badly, if that is the only way it gets answered.

307
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:54,070
I am going to open the conversation I have been avoiding, and I am going to open it gently, and I am not going to open it to win.

308
00:20:54,070 --> 00:20:58,770
I am going to speak to that person in a different voice than the one I used yesterday.

309
00:20:58,770 --> 00:21:00,620
Not a performance.

310
00:21:00,620 --> 00:21:04,270
Just a lower voice and a longer pause before I answer.

311
00:21:04,270 --> 00:21:08,890
And I am going to make the decision instead of circling it for another day.

312
00:21:08,890 --> 00:21:11,360
I have asked you for the next step.

313
00:21:11,360 --> 00:21:16,740
I am not going to stand still, waiting for a road I can see all the way to the end.

314
00:21:16,740 --> 00:21:19,940
If I get it wrong, you will correct me.

315
00:21:19,940 --> 00:21:23,210
That is not a risk I am taking alone.

316
00:21:23,210 --> 00:21:26,040
And now something in me has gone quiet.

317
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:29,240
Not because the day got easier while I was praying.

318
00:21:29,240 --> 00:21:30,770
It did not.

319
00:21:30,770 --> 00:21:34,190
Everything I walked in here with is still true.

320
00:21:34,190 --> 00:21:38,840
But I have heard something now, and it was not the voice I woke up to.

321
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:42,990
The one that read yesterday back to me is on the floor where I left it.

322
00:21:42,990 --> 00:21:44,560
It can talk.

323
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:46,750
It cannot go first anymore.

324
00:21:46,750 --> 00:21:55,940
I know who spoke first this morning, and I know what you said, and I am going to be carrying that around all day whether or not I feel it by noon.

325
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:57,490
It is enough.

326
00:21:57,490 --> 00:21:59,390
It is more than enough.

327
00:21:59,390 --> 00:22:01,900
It is quiet in here now.

328
00:22:01,900 --> 00:22:09,340
You were speaking before I woke, and you will still be speaking after I close this and step into the noise.

329
00:22:09,340 --> 00:22:12,220
That is not something I arranged this morning.

330
00:22:12,220 --> 00:22:14,170
It is who you are.

331
00:22:14,170 --> 00:22:17,110
It has been true since before I had a name.

332
00:22:17,110 --> 00:22:27,040
Your love did not begin when I finally quieted down enough to hear it, and it will not end when I get distracted at nine o'clock and forget I prayed.

333
00:22:27,040 --> 00:22:30,590
I came in here losing an argument I did not start.

334
00:22:30,590 --> 00:22:36,350
The voice that was reading my failures back to me is still in the building, and it is no longer the first one.

335
00:22:36,350 --> 00:22:41,740
Nothing about my day has changed, and everything about who is speaking into it has.

336
00:22:41,740 --> 00:22:43,800
I am not hurried anymore.

337
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:45,620
I am not alone in it.

338
00:22:45,620 --> 00:22:48,051
I know which way to take the next step.

339
00:22:48,051 --> 00:22:53,951
And I ask all of this through Jesus, who made it possible for a morning like this to happen,

340
00:22:53,951 --> 00:22:58,771
who brought me near so that I am heard as a child and not as a stranger.

341
00:22:58,771 --> 00:23:01,231
And now, for the one listening.

342
00:23:01,231 --> 00:23:04,731
May the first voice you hear tomorrow be his.

343
00:23:04,731 --> 00:23:09,371
May his mercy meet you before your feet touch the floor.

344
00:23:09,371 --> 00:23:14,951
May you be given the one step you need at the hour you need it, and not one hour late.

345
00:23:14,951 --> 00:23:19,131
May you be kept steady in the room where nothing has changed yet.

346
00:23:19,131 --> 00:23:29,741
And may the love that spoke over you this morning still be speaking over you tonight, when the house is quiet and you are alone with your thoughts again.

347
00:23:29,741 --> 00:23:33,251
Take one more breath here before you go.

348
00:23:33,251 --> 00:23:40,021
When you are ready, open your eyes, and carry this morning with you instead of leaving it in this room.

349
00:23:40,021 --> 00:23:42,991
In Jesus' name we pray, amen.

350
00:23:42,991 --> 00:23:45,401
Stay in that quiet for a second.

351
00:23:45,401 --> 00:23:48,831
It will follow you further into today than you think.

352
00:23:48,831 --> 00:23:52,721
Before you go, one word in the comments.

353
00:23:52,721 --> 00:23:55,201
Just write, listening.

354
00:23:55,201 --> 00:23:56,661
That is all.

355
00:23:56,661 --> 00:24:02,151
It tells me you were here this morning, and I will pray for the name beside it today.

356
00:24:02,151 --> 00:24:11,291
If this morning helped you, leave a like so it reaches someone who is praying alone this morning, and send it to the one person you thought of while we prayed.

357
00:24:11,291 --> 00:24:15,986
There is one more line in David's prayer that we did not touch today.

358
00:24:15,986 --> 00:24:19,866
After asking for love and direction, he asked for something harder.

359
00:24:19,866 --> 00:24:22,406
Hearing his voice first is one thing.

360
00:24:22,406 --> 00:24:27,166
Walking out into a day that already has something against you is another.

361
00:24:27,166 --> 00:24:31,176
That is Psalm one hundred forty-three, verse nine.

362
00:24:31,176 --> 00:24:37,466
We start the day with God together tomorrow morning, before you say anything else to anyone.

363
00:24:37,466 --> 00:24:39,646
I will be here early.
